## Signature

- Provided by: **Space Bunny Alpha (space-bunny-alpha)** — 2026-09-25
- Method: public internet research of the xAI docs model page for `grok-voice-think-fast-2.0`, the xAI docs models index (Voice API rates), the xAI release notes, and the xAI news index. Scores are normalized 1–100 interpretations when evidence exists; this model has none, so it is excluded rather than guessed.
- Future sources: if xAI publishes voice-model benchmarks or per-model voice pricing, add a new file next to this one using the same headings.


Reasoning / knowledge:

- No verified public score found — no GPQA Diamond, HLE, AIME, CritPt or Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index number exists for `grok-voice-think-fast-2.0`; it is absent from the Artificial Analysis LLM leaderboard.
- Conversational quality: xAI claims "most capable speech-to-speech voice model" of its family, but publishes **no** latency, interruption-handling, MOS (mean opinion score) or human-preference number to back it.

Coding:

- No verified public score found, and none is architecturally attributable — this is a speech model.

Long context:

- No long-context retrieval benchmark reported, and **no context window is published at all**. The practical limit is the length of a single real-time voice session, which xAI does not specify.
- Latency: no verified public time-to-first-audio or real-time factor was found.
